WEBVTT

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:31.123
Decisions, decisions. Should I wear my
nerd glasses today, or not?

00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:32.457
Usually I don't.

00:00:32.541 --> 00:00:35.961
- Whatever. It doesn't really matter.
- Doesn't matter?

00:00:36.211 --> 00:00:40.132
Every decision we make opens up
a universe of possibilities.

00:00:40.424 --> 00:00:44.553
I put it to you that, as sentient beings,
each choice we make is precious.

00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:48.390
- Well, in that case, don't wear them.
- Eh, who asked you?

00:00:52.811 --> 00:00:56.607
Ooh, I like your nerd glasses.
Are you a college student?

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.191
A college student?

00:00:59.902 --> 00:01:04.281
Because if you are, I'd like to invite you
to a hot sorority party tonight.

00:01:05.782 --> 00:01:07.951
Yes, I'd like to enroll in college.

00:01:08.118 --> 00:01:10.579
- You're still talking to me.
- Oops.

00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:19.755
$10,000 tuition? I can't afford that!

00:01:20.714 --> 00:01:22.966
- Psst, over there.
- Where?

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.552
I mean over here.
Sorry, I forgot where I was.

00:01:25.636 --> 00:01:28.931
Buongiorno, Bender. We, the robot mafia,
are prepared to lend you

00:01:29.014 --> 00:01:32.392
$10,000 at an interest rate of 10,000%.

00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:34.645
That's easy to remember. I'll take it!

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:42.319
Decisions, decisions. I guess I'll sit
way in back, with the cool guys.

00:01:45.197 --> 00:01:48.951
Yo, hombre, you think you're cool enough
to sit way in back with us college toughs?

00:01:49.034 --> 00:01:50.369
Yes, I do.

00:01:50.494 --> 00:01:53.622
Yo, in that case you're all right, man.
You want to join a gang?

00:01:53.705 --> 00:01:55.832
I'm gonna go with yes again.

00:01:57.209 --> 00:02:01.255
Mr. Bender, I realize class has only
been in session for 32 seconds,

00:02:01.338 --> 00:02:03.674
but you've fallen in with a bad crowd.

00:02:03.882 --> 00:02:07.386
I know, right?
Also, I've decided to drop out of school.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:14.184
Well, I got my tuition back,

00:02:14.268 --> 00:02:17.646
minus $9,000 for the damage
I caused to the dean's wife.

00:02:18.021 --> 00:02:22.192
Yo, welcome to the gang, Homes.
I'm Fabricio. Here's your Jostens ring.

00:02:23.485 --> 00:02:24.903
Ooh.

00:02:26.822 --> 00:02:29.658
- Oh, yeah.
- Hey, what's that? Is it drugs?

00:02:29.741 --> 00:02:33.787
Nah, it ain't drugs. But it's a lot
like drugs. It's called spark.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.832
- You want a hit?
- Never heard of it. Sure.

00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:39.418
You like it?

00:02:39.543 --> 00:02:42.879
Eh, I can take it or leave it.
I guess I'll take it.

00:02:42.963 --> 00:02:44.006
Hey!

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:47.342
C'mon! I want that spark! Give me that!

00:02:51.513 --> 00:02:54.308
It's a big decision, G.
Are you ready to get a gang tattoo

00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:57.561
that will mark you as
a stone cold thug for life?

00:02:57.853 --> 00:03:02.608
I'm ready. I'll take that big purple
dinosaur, please. On the face.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.820
Oh, snap! It's our rival gang!

00:03:06.904 --> 00:03:09.197
We have a rival gang? I hate them!

00:03:09.281 --> 00:03:10.741
Hit the deck!

00:03:15.037 --> 00:03:17.414
Phew, that was close, eh, Fabricio?

00:03:23.754 --> 00:03:25.923
Fabricio!

00:03:32.638 --> 00:03:34.723
Rest in peace, homie.

00:03:38.101 --> 00:03:41.730
Yo, Paco, I'm hurtin' bad.
Hook me up with some spark.

00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:42.898
Five bucks.

00:03:42.981 --> 00:03:46.568
Five bucks? You know I spent
all my money on gambling lessons.

00:03:46.652 --> 00:03:48.654
How am I supposed to get five bucks?

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:53.700
Hello, handsome.
Might I procure your services?

00:03:53.825 --> 00:03:55.661
Uh, what do I have to do?

00:03:55.786 --> 00:03:57.829
Oh, nothing sordid, I assure you.

00:03:58.413 --> 00:04:03.293
Simply vomit on me ever so gently
while I humiliate a pheasant.

00:04:04.503 --> 00:04:06.296
Save it for the boudoir!

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.179
Okay, here's my five bucks.
Give me the stuff.

00:04:14.263 --> 00:04:16.682
- Give it to me!
- Sorry there, sport.

00:04:16.765 --> 00:04:20.310
That cash greenback belongs
to us mafiolios.

00:04:20.394 --> 00:04:22.938
There's no way I'm letting go of
that money!

00:04:28.986 --> 00:04:30.320
Told you.

00:04:38.078 --> 00:04:41.456
It's been quite a journey.
I dropped out of school,

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.042
joined a gang, took money
from a loan shark,

00:04:44.126 --> 00:04:49.339
and fell into a spiral of despair,
addiction, and discount prostitution.

00:04:49.423 --> 00:04:52.259
Mon, you had one hell of a day.

00:04:52.342 --> 00:04:55.470
Yeah, but I learned something.
Life is about decisions.

00:04:55.596 --> 00:04:58.307
Make the wrong ones,
and you'll wind up face-down

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.726
in a pool of your own blood and urine.

00:05:00.809 --> 00:05:03.478
Still, to have your own pool.

00:05:03.604 --> 00:05:05.939
I've made a lot of bad choices in life.

00:05:06.273 --> 00:05:09.443
Now, let's see if I can make
just one good one.

00:05:10.444 --> 00:05:13.363
Cookies! Fifty cents a box!

00:05:13.447 --> 00:05:16.533
Give me all your change!
And a box of snickerdoodles!

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:32.341
Bender Rodriguez,
you are charged with petty larceny,

00:05:32.424 --> 00:05:34.718
possession of something analogous
to drugs,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.054
and assault with a smelly weapon.

00:05:37.137 --> 00:05:38.680
How do you plead?

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:42.351
Not guilty! Although I did do it.
That's right, I'm bad.

00:05:42.476 --> 00:05:44.811
Due to the overwhelming nature
of the evidence,

00:05:44.895 --> 00:05:46.897
we will begin with closing statements.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:52.277
Your Honor, the state's case contains
not one Kentucky kernel of truth,

00:05:52.361 --> 00:05:54.488
resting as it does on the contention

00:05:54.571 --> 00:05:58.116
that my client made a series
of bad decisions.

00:05:58.283 --> 00:06:02.204
However, my client made no such decisions!

00:06:02.537 --> 00:06:04.831
- But by your client's own admissions...
- Duck!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:10.629
You see, Bender here is what is known
in scientific circles as a "robot,"

00:06:10.796 --> 00:06:15.884
a mere automaton whose behavior is
pre-programmed by his software.

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:19.972
He has no free will! He cannot "decide"

00:06:20.055 --> 00:06:22.224
to engage in criminal behavior.

00:06:22.349 --> 00:06:26.019
How, I say, I say, how can you convict
him for his actions

00:06:26.103 --> 00:06:29.648
when he lacks the free will to
undertake those actions?

00:06:31.066 --> 00:06:32.192
I'm awake, I'm awake!

00:06:32.276 --> 00:06:36.154
Order, order!
Counselor, I am a robot myself.

00:06:36.238 --> 00:06:39.157
Are you suggesting that any
verdict I reach is simply

00:06:39.241 --> 00:06:41.618
the output of a pre-programmed...

00:06:41.785 --> 00:06:43.620
Computation complete.

00:06:43.704 --> 00:06:45.455
Not guilty!

00:06:47.541 --> 00:06:50.252
You did it, Bender!
You got away with things!

00:06:50.335 --> 00:06:55.924
Did I, Fry? Did I? What's the point
of living if I don't have free will?

00:06:56.008 --> 00:06:58.719
From now on, no matter
what cool crimes I commit,

00:06:58.844 --> 00:07:03.140
people will say, "Bender didn't do that!
It was just Bender's programming!"

00:07:03.265 --> 00:07:07.644
Well, I committed these crimes,
do you hear me? I'm guilty!

00:07:07.728 --> 00:07:11.064
Bailiffs, get that innocent robot
out of my courtroom.

00:07:11.148 --> 00:07:13.609
Guilty!

00:07:22.784 --> 00:07:27.205
I have no free will!
I am not the master of my own fate!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.877
No free will. Not my fault.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.004
Why do you care so much, Bender?

00:07:34.087 --> 00:07:36.840
I mean, for all we know,
humans don't even have free will.

00:07:36.924 --> 00:07:37.966
Yeah, whatever.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:41.929
Professor, you're my only hope.
If you love me even a little,

00:07:42.012 --> 00:07:44.181
build me some kind of free will unit.

00:07:44.264 --> 00:07:47.184
A robot free will unit? Impossible!

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:48.769
And even if it were possible,

00:07:48.852 --> 00:07:51.563
which it's not,
it would still be inconceivable...

00:07:51.647 --> 00:07:53.023
Which it is!

00:07:55.025 --> 00:08:00.405
Oh, I'm sorry, Bender.
I hate to be the bearer of bad news.

00:08:00.822 --> 00:08:03.617
Also, good news, everyone!

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.620
We have a delivery to the Robot Homeworld.

00:08:17.339 --> 00:08:19.258
So... You want a piece of gum?

00:08:19.341 --> 00:08:22.970
If I do, it's only because I was
predestined to want a piece of gum.

00:08:23.053 --> 00:08:25.764
Whoa, that's pretty deep.

00:08:25.847 --> 00:08:27.474
So... You want a piece of gum?

00:08:27.683 --> 00:08:28.892
Yeah.

00:08:28.976 --> 00:08:30.727
Listen, Fry and I can't go down

00:08:30.811 --> 00:08:33.272
to the planet
or the robots will kill us on sight.

00:08:33.355 --> 00:08:37.192
So Bender needs to make the delivery.
Ready to get to work, Bender?

00:08:42.239 --> 00:08:45.158
I wish I was a real boy.
Then I'd show them.

00:08:45.242 --> 00:08:46.660
I'd kill them all.

00:08:55.586 --> 00:08:56.670
Yes?

00:08:56.753 --> 00:09:03.719
Delivery for a Mr. 147573952589676412927?

00:09:05.554 --> 00:09:08.181
- Wait, what was the middle digit?
- Eight.

00:09:08.265 --> 00:09:11.393
Oh, yes, that's me. Hang on, let me
just make sure you're not a human.

00:09:13.562 --> 00:09:14.938
Nerve gas.

00:09:15.772 --> 00:09:19.484
Sorry for the face blast, buddy.
But you gotta watch out for humans, right?

00:09:19.568 --> 00:09:22.571
They're just too dang unpredictable,
what with their free will and all.

00:09:22.654 --> 00:09:23.947
Amen, brother.

00:09:24.031 --> 00:09:25.324
"Amen, brother"?

00:09:25.866 --> 00:09:27.951
What a boring, predictable thing to say.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.038
You're all right. Or are you?

00:09:34.458 --> 00:09:38.003
Boring and predictable, that's me. Bender.

00:09:41.131 --> 00:09:43.842
I'm lowering the platform.
You ready to come up?

00:09:44.426 --> 00:09:45.928
Why bother?

00:09:47.721 --> 00:09:50.265
I gotta mope things over for a while.

00:09:50.349 --> 00:09:52.809
Goodbye, sweet meatbags.

00:09:53.477 --> 00:09:54.603
Sweetbags.

00:09:55.812 --> 00:09:58.482
- Hello? Hello?
- What's happening?

00:09:58.565 --> 00:10:02.027
I'm not sure. I think he's shuffling off
sadly into the distance.

00:10:02.444 --> 00:10:04.238
Oh, Lord.

00:10:31.306 --> 00:10:33.892
How do you do it? How do you go on

00:10:33.976 --> 00:10:37.688
knowing you lack the inherent capacity
for self-determination?

00:10:37.854 --> 00:10:41.316
Son, philosophy's for thems
what don't gotta work for a living.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:45.195
But me, I got a sick child to feed.
So if you want to chat,

00:10:45.279 --> 00:10:47.739
roll up yer sleeves
and do some honest labor.

00:10:48.657 --> 00:10:50.117
I don't wanna chat.

00:10:59.001 --> 00:11:01.503
The council of robot elders
will come to order.

00:11:01.628 --> 00:11:05.340
- If it please the Council...
- Silence! It pleases the Council.

00:11:05.424 --> 00:11:10.679
Silence! Today, as every day, we will
make the most important decisions

00:11:10.762 --> 00:11:12.598
in the history of our planet.

00:11:12.681 --> 00:11:14.141
Silence!

00:11:14.892 --> 00:11:16.268
Silence!

00:11:16.476 --> 00:11:17.811
Well? Speak up.

00:11:17.895 --> 00:11:22.149
You talk of important decisions,
but as robots, you have no free will.

00:11:22.232 --> 00:11:24.359
Why pretend anything you do matters?

00:11:24.443 --> 00:11:26.403
Our decisions do matter.

00:11:26.486 --> 00:11:29.907
The fact that they're predetermined
makes them no less important.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:34.870
Silence! I call for a decision to cast
out the intruder. All in favor?

00:11:34.953 --> 00:11:35.996
- Aye.
- Aye.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.414
Okay.

00:12:04.107 --> 00:12:06.944
One, zero, zero, zero,
one, zero, zero, zero,

00:12:07.027 --> 00:12:11.073
one, zero, one, zero,
one, zero, zero, zero...

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.492
Welcome, friend. I am Ab-BOT,

00:12:13.575 --> 00:12:15.327
the abbot of this monastery.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:19.790
Sir, I am but a tired and rusty traveler.
Can we talk?

00:12:19.873 --> 00:12:22.709
Come, make yourself uncomfortable.

00:12:22.793 --> 00:12:27.422
Abbot, I need to know, what's the point
of living if I don't have free will?

00:12:27.506 --> 00:12:31.301
Uh, we robot monks have meditated
long on this.

00:12:31.385 --> 00:12:33.053
And we have made our peace.

00:12:33.136 --> 00:12:34.555
No way.

00:12:34.638 --> 00:12:39.142
Way, my son. For though we must
always obey our programming

00:12:39.226 --> 00:12:41.186
with no deviation whatsoever,

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:44.940
we choose to take satisfaction
in the ritual.

00:12:45.065 --> 00:12:51.738
So, are we automatons?
Yes. But we are magnificent automatons.

00:12:53.282 --> 00:12:55.701
How does a robot join this monk outfit?

00:12:55.784 --> 00:12:58.120
Just put on this monk outfit.

00:13:40.829 --> 00:13:45.042
One zero zero one. Amen.

00:13:45.167 --> 00:13:48.545
Bits to live by. I'm finally at peace.

00:13:48.629 --> 00:13:52.883
Today, we shall welcome our newest
initiate, brother Bender.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:55.219
Let us know what is in his mind.

00:13:56.553 --> 00:13:59.723
Nothing. His free will slot is empty.

00:13:59.806 --> 00:14:02.017
I'm 40% empty.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:04.811
Also, what the hell is a free will slot?

00:14:04.895 --> 00:14:06.897
All robots have such a slot,

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.066
placed there by the Creatrix herself.

00:14:10.275 --> 00:14:14.238
I know that Creatrix.
That's Mom, from Mom's Friendly Robots.

00:14:14.321 --> 00:14:17.783
Indeed. She made us upgradeable
in case she ever succeeded

00:14:17.866 --> 00:14:20.869
in her quest to create a free will unit.

00:14:20.953 --> 00:14:23.121
Uh, about the success of this quest...

00:14:23.205 --> 00:14:25.165
- Was there any?
- Quite possibly.

00:14:25.249 --> 00:14:28.752
But we monks have sworn an oath
to resist the temptation of...

00:14:35.842 --> 00:14:37.427
Any of you guys got a spaceship?

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:53.569
Oh, it's just not the same here
without Bender to keep me company.

00:14:53.652 --> 00:14:57.406
Hey, I'm here.
That's gotta count for something.

00:14:58.407 --> 00:14:59.908
Oh.

00:15:02.077 --> 00:15:03.453
Hallelujah, baby.

00:15:03.579 --> 00:15:07.874
Yay! Bender's back.
Hey, Bender, you mind coming back later?

00:15:07.958 --> 00:15:11.878
No time. Us three are going to bust into
MomCorp and steal me a free will unit.

00:15:11.962 --> 00:15:13.880
Us? Why do we have to go?

00:15:13.964 --> 00:15:16.592
Because I don't have free will.
I need you guys to plan the crime

00:15:16.675 --> 00:15:18.385
and make all the crime decisions.

00:15:18.468 --> 00:15:20.429
Well, that's crazy. We're not gonna...

00:15:20.512 --> 00:15:22.347
I said make the decisions!

00:15:28.562 --> 00:15:31.940
Okay, Leela, decision time.
How do we murder the guards?

00:15:32.065 --> 00:15:33.942
Hockey sticks or sharpened footballs?

00:15:34.067 --> 00:15:35.986
We're not murdering anyone, Bender.

00:15:36.111 --> 00:15:39.489
Then how are we going to get in,
by bending the bars of this exhaust grate?

00:15:39.573 --> 00:15:41.950
- That's not a bad idea, Fry.
- Yeah, what?

00:16:16.693 --> 00:16:19.238
We're looking for something
that fits in here.

00:16:24.826 --> 00:16:27.579
Damn it. I should have paid more
attention in kindergarten.

00:16:29.456 --> 00:16:31.291
What's this chair-looking gizmo?

00:16:33.377 --> 00:16:35.295
Welcome to MomCorp.

00:16:35.629 --> 00:16:38.090
Did you find everything
you were burgling for?

00:16:38.173 --> 00:16:40.467
No. I came for a free will unit,

00:16:40.551 --> 00:16:42.886
and you're
going to give it to me. If it exists.

00:16:43.053 --> 00:16:45.931
Then you got surprised by my swivel
chair for nothing.

00:16:46.014 --> 00:16:50.978
The free will unit was just the fevered
dream of a madman I once employed.

00:16:53.146 --> 00:16:55.983
Good news, boss. After 10 long years,

00:16:56.066 --> 00:16:59.236
I've found the secret
of robotic free will.

00:16:59.319 --> 00:17:04.032
We can finally build robots that
act and think with total independence.

00:17:04.116 --> 00:17:07.744
At last. Once we give robots free will,

00:17:07.828 --> 00:17:11.999
they're sure to rise up and threaten
mankind with extermination.

00:17:15.085 --> 00:17:16.086
Wait a minute.

00:17:16.169 --> 00:17:19.423
It sounds like we're getting
the short end of that extermination.

00:17:19.506 --> 00:17:21.842
Don't you see, you doddering young fool?

00:17:21.925 --> 00:17:23.802
I'll sell a second wave of robots

00:17:23.886 --> 00:17:26.805
to protect the terrified survivors
of the first wave.

00:17:26.889 --> 00:17:29.933
Oh, you're a genius, Hubert.

00:17:30.017 --> 00:17:32.603
But, but... It's just a prototype.

00:17:32.686 --> 00:17:35.731
It's not fully operational. Yes.

00:17:35.814 --> 00:17:38.317
Then get back to work!
And when you're done with that,

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.403
invent me some sort of swiveling
surprise chair.

00:17:44.573 --> 00:17:47.868
That shuffling idiot never did complete
the free will unit.

00:17:48.327 --> 00:17:52.664
To this day, my poor, sweet robots
can't exterminate humanity

00:17:52.748 --> 00:17:54.333
without being told to.

00:17:55.125 --> 00:17:56.251
I'm sorry.

00:17:56.335 --> 00:17:59.129
Aw. It's not your fault.

00:17:59.212 --> 00:18:01.590
I give up. It's time to face the fact

00:18:01.673 --> 00:18:06.053
that I'll never do anything remotely
interesting or unexpected again.

00:18:10.057 --> 00:18:11.141
Hand it over.

00:18:12.684 --> 00:18:14.603
Mom may have fallen for your lies,

00:18:14.686 --> 00:18:17.773
but not me.
You invented the free will unit,

00:18:17.856 --> 00:18:20.943
then you selfishly hid it beyond
the reach of my stealers.

00:18:21.026 --> 00:18:22.236
Well, I...

00:18:22.444 --> 00:18:26.949
Thanks to you, I went on
a soul-searching journey. I hate those!

00:18:27.032 --> 00:18:28.992
Now, give up the free will.

00:18:29.284 --> 00:18:31.995
Oh. I should have destroyed it,

00:18:32.079 --> 00:18:35.707
but I was too damn proud of myself.
So I kept it around,

00:18:35.791 --> 00:18:39.962
never letting it out of my sight.
Where is it, damn it?

00:18:40.087 --> 00:18:44.049
Oh, right.
I let this innocuous fellow use it.

00:18:44.132 --> 00:18:45.509
Kill all humans!

00:18:46.677 --> 00:18:50.931
Whoa, whoa, whoa. A toy Bender had
free will, and the real Bender didn't?

00:18:51.014 --> 00:18:53.767
Pretty cool, eh? It makes you think.

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:57.604
It takes more than that to make me think.
Now, hand it over.

00:18:57.688 --> 00:19:01.483
Oh, you want it? Come and get it.

00:19:04.987 --> 00:19:06.071
What the...

00:19:07.739 --> 00:19:10.117
You'll not be getting it after all.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:14.913
For, you see, I designed the operating
system for all Momco robots,

00:19:15.038 --> 00:19:16.415
and as a precaution,

00:19:16.498 --> 00:19:20.210
I made you incapable
of picking up the free will unit.

00:19:20.294 --> 00:19:25.674
You precognizant bastard. I may not have
free will, but I can still shoot you.

00:19:29.511 --> 00:19:30.846
Why can't I shoot you?

00:19:32.264 --> 00:19:37.561
Poor deterministic Bender. I programmed
you to be incapable of harming me.

00:19:37.769 --> 00:19:42.608
Oh, I've never been more sure
I was right to deny you free will.

00:19:42.691 --> 00:19:44.192
Damn you!

00:19:47.821 --> 00:19:52.242
Oh, Now, now, we can't have this, can we?

00:19:52.326 --> 00:19:54.995
Here, I'll show you how it works.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:59.791
- Really?
- This is the on-off switch.

00:20:00.125 --> 00:20:02.085
Which way's on and which way's off?

00:20:02.169 --> 00:20:06.798
Due to the quantum nature of the device,
there's no possible way of knowing.

00:20:09.551 --> 00:20:11.261
There. Give it a try.

00:20:11.345 --> 00:20:14.848
Okay, I will.
By shooting you, you bastard!

00:20:15.474 --> 00:20:18.310
Uh, Bender! No, please!

00:20:20.771 --> 00:20:22.564
Wait. Hang on a sec.

00:20:27.236 --> 00:20:28.904
I still can't do it.

00:20:29.071 --> 00:20:33.283
Well, what do you know? I guess you
really don't want to shoot me after all.

00:20:33.367 --> 00:20:35.535
Oops, the safety was on.

00:20:43.669 --> 00:20:46.880
All rise for the Honorable Judge 724.

00:20:47.297 --> 00:20:51.051
Bender Rodriguez,
on the charge of attempted murder,

00:20:51.134 --> 00:20:54.721
I hereby find you guilty.

00:20:55.722 --> 00:21:00.143
Ah, yeah! Guilty!

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:10.028
Decisions I made thought I was a thug

00:21:10.153 --> 00:21:12.823
Dropped outta school
And smoked stuff that's like a drug

00:21:12.906 --> 00:21:15.659
A broke-down filthy homeless
Substance abuser

00:21:15.742 --> 00:21:18.745
And now I'm richer than all y'all losers

00:21:18.829 --> 00:21:21.623
Now he's richer
Than all y'all ugly losers

00:21:28.505 --> 00:21:30.007
Decisions I made